# Oldest PipelineC (JulianKemmerer/PipelineC) commit this design is known to
# work with. This commit or any newer one should work; prefer the latest.
# CI builds the Pypeline lint with it (.github/workflows/lint.yml), and
# build.py warns when the local pypelinec checkout predates it.
# Move it forward in the same commit as any design change that needs a newer
# PipelineC. The first line that is not a comment is the hash.
# Requires simulation-only @MAINs (@MAIN over @sim_input/@sim_output), used by
# the native testbenches; native sim casting every wire write to the wire's type
# (PipelineC#392: the testbenches write plain ints, port_waves packs them);
# a PipelineC that imports without distutils (CI runs Python 3.12); and
# --module_prefix (PipelineC#400), which build.py --enc and --dec pass.
